** (without vowel harmony) {{IPA|pt|/pɔˈde(h)/}}
* {{IPA|pt|/puˈde(ɹ)/|a=Rural Central Brazil}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|po|der}}

====Verb====
{{pt-verb}}

# {{senseid|pt|to have the ability to}} {{lb|pt|auxiliary}} to [[be able]] to; [[can]] {{gl|to have the ability to}} {{+obj|pt|inf}}
#: {{syn|pt|conseguir}}
#: {{ux|pt|Eu '''posso''' arrumar isso.|I '''can''' fix this.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to have the permission to}} {{lb|pt|auxiliary}} [[can]]; to be [[allowed]] to {{gl|to have the permission to}} {{+obj|pt|inf}}
#: {{ux|pt|Não '''podem''' ficar no pátio.|You '''can’t''' stay in the patio.}}
# {{senseid|pt|it is possible that}} {{lb|pt|auxiliary}} [[can]]; [[could]] {{q|indicates possibility}} {{+obj|pt|inf}}
#: {{ux|pt|O montanhista '''podia''' cair a qualquer momento.|The climber '''could''' fall at any moment.}}
# {{lb|pt|auxiliary}} [[may]]; [[might]] {{gl|indicates possibility but uncertainty}} {{+obj|pt|inf}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''Pode''' ser que eu vá.|I '''might''' go.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to be able to take on}} {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to be able to [[take on]] {{gl|to be able to defeat or withstand}} {{+obj|pt|:com<someone>}}
#: {{ux|pt|Ninguém '''pode''' comigo!|No one '''can take''' me '''on'''!}}
# {{senseid|pt|to be allowed}} {{lb|pt|informal|intransitive}} to be [[allowed]]
#: {{ux|pt|Comer aqui '''pode'''.|Eating here '''is allowed'''.}}
# {{lb|pt|informal|intransitive}} to be available for a meeting or appointment
#: {{ux|pt|Eu '''posso''' terça.|I'm available on Tuesday.}}

